rgames.com/w/b/s/family-relics.webp"><img src="https://media.silvergames.com/j/b/s/family-relics.jpg" alt="family relics" width="140" height="140" loading="lazy"></picture></a></div><div class="game-teaser-txt"><a href="/en/family-relics">Family Nest: Family Relics</a></div></div>  </div> <button class="scroll" type="button" data-scroll="sd10" aria-label="Scroll right">&#10095;</button> </div> </section>  </div>  </main> <!-- Legacy's footer is `<br>` + ONE line + `<br>`, and the two rules are the
         whole of its spacing — `.footer` carries no padding (main.css). --> <footer class="footer" dir="ltr"> <br> <div> <!-- No colon here: translation 71 already ends in one in all 47 locales
             (`Language:`, `Sprache:`, `لغة:`), so adding a literal `: ` printed
             `Language::` on every page in every language. --> <label for="language_select">Language: </label> <!-- Static site, so the switch is wired in site.ts: it rewrites only the
             language segment, keeping the visitor on the same page. --> <select id="language_select" data-language-switch data-language="en" data-slug> <option value="en" selected>English</option><option value="de">Deutsch</option><option value="es">Español</option><option value="fr">Français</option><option value="br">Português</option><option value="bs">Bosanski</option><option value="cs">Čeština</option><option value="da">Dansk</option><option value="et">Eesti keel</option><option value="tl">Filipino</option><option value="it">Italiano</option><option value="do">Indonesia</option><option value="hr">Hrvatski</option><option value="lv">Latviski</option><option value="lt">Lietuvis</option><option value="hu">Magyar</option><option value="ms">Malaysia</option><option value="nl">Nederlands</option><option value="nb">Norsk</option><option value="pl">Polski</option><option value="ro">Română</option><option value="fi">Suomi</option><option value="sl">Slovenščina</option><option value="sk">Slovenský</option><option value="sv">Svenska</option><option value="sq">Shqiptare</option><option value="vi">Tiếng Việt</option><option value="tr">Türkçe</option><option value="el">Ελληνικά</option><option value="kk">Қазақ</option><option value="bg">български</option><option value="mk">македонски</option><option value="uk">Українська</option><option value="ru">Русский</option><option value="sr">Српски</option><option value="ja">日本</option><option value="ko">한국인</option><option value="th">แบบไทย</option><option value="hi">हिंदी</option><option value="mr">मराठी</option><option value="gu">ગુજરાતી</option><option value="pa">ਪੰਜਾਬੀ</option><option value="bn">বাংলা</option><option value="zh">中国人</option><option value="ur">اردو</option><option value="ar">عربي</option><option value="fa">فارسی</option> </select>
&nbsp; www.silvergames.com
<!-- INLINE, on this same line, in legacy's own order — `footerText` (row
             76) reads `www.silvergames.com | Scholarship | Submit a game | About
             us | Terms of Use | Privacy Settings`. The separators come from
             `.footer-pages a::before`, so the run reads identically whichever
             slugs resolve.

             `3` renders as the CONSENT BUTTON rather than a link to its page:
             production's `/site/3` IS its cookie-settings UI (`static.php:17`
             loads `cookie_settings_script.html` there), and this port's
             equivalent control is the banner re-opener. Same label, same
             position, one occurrence — linking the page as well would print
             "Privacy Settings" twice on a line production shows once. --> <span class="footer-pages">  | <a href="/en/site/scholarship">Scholarship</a> | <a href="/en/site/submit-a-game">Submit a game</a> | <a href="/en/site/1">About us</a> | <a href="/en/site/2">Terms of Use</a> | <button type="button" data-consent-reopen>Privacy Settings</button> </span> </div> <br> <!-- Legacy has no copyright line at all (CU-86ajwdxcv). The year is emitted at
           BUILD time for crawlers and no-JS clients, then re-read by
           initCopyrightYear() in site.ts — one shell is built once and the Worker
           caches its composed responses, so a build-time-only year would still say
           2026 on 1 January. `rights` is authored English with no legacy translation
           row, so the other 46 locales compose the baked English fallback until an MT
           batch fills data/mt-ui-strings.json. --> <p class="footer-copyright">
© <span data-copyright-year>2026</span> Silvergames.com. All rights reserved. </p> </footer> <!-- Shown only when decideConsent() says one is required. Markup is always
         present; /geo decides at runtime. --> <aside data-consent-banner role="dialog" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Cookie consent"> <div class="consent-inner"> <p>We and our partners use cookies to personalise content and ads, and to measure their performance. You can accept all cookies or continue with only the ones needed to run the site.</p> <button class="consent-btn" type="button" data-consent="essential">Only essential</button> <button class="consent-btn" type="button" data-consent="all">Accept all</button> </div> </aside> </body></html>